# Blues Turnarounds in E and A (repertoire plan: st-blues-turnarounds). An original study on the
# traditional 12-bar form. A turnaround fills bars 11 and 12 and leads back to the top.
# In E: over the open string 6, a line falls by half steps on string 3, fret 7 (D), 6 (C#),
# 5 (C), 4 (B), one note per beat, each struck with the open string 1 (E) as a swung long-short
# pair; bar 12 is B7 (x21202). In A: over the open string 5, the same on string 4, fret 5 (G),
# 4 (F#), 3 (F), 2 (E), with the open string 1; bar 12 is E7 (020100). Both lines run b7, 6, b6, 5.
# Left hand: fingers 4, 3, 2, 1, one per fret. Right hand: thumb (P) on the bass of beat 1,
# i on the moving note, a on string 1. Then a full 12-bar chorus with each one, using the shuffle
# from the 12-bar study (played with the thumb), and a last chord to finish.
# Swung eighths are written as triplets: q3 (long) then e3 (short) in each beat.
title: Blues Turnarounds in E and A
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the traditional 12-bar blues form
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
